  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 07/03/2025 the proposal as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 07/03/2025 and numbered SHA-DR-24-05-11-16 Rev A02, SHA-DR-24-05-11-17 Rev A02, SHA-DR-24-05-11-13 Rev A02, SHA-DR-24-05-11-18 Rev A02, SHA-DR-24-05-11-14 Rev A02, SHA-DR-24-05-11-15 Rev A02, was not lawful within the meanings of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 because: \r\n\r\nThe development fails to comply with the terms of Class A, Clauses A.1 (f), A.1 (j) and A.2 (b) of Part 1, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015 (as amended) because the application site is located on article 2(3) land and the proposal would extend beyond a wall forming a side elevation of the original dwelling house and would measure more than half the width of the original dwellinghouse and would extend beyond the rear wall of the original dwellinghouse by more than 3 metres. Planning permission is therefore required.\r\n\r\n"
